  "abstract": "Library-reference skill for open-source MLflow 3, scoped to classic-ML MLOps. 24 rules across 6 categories covering the decisions where MLflow 3 broke with the MLflow 2 idioms a model produces by default: named LoggedModels instead of run-artifact models, registry aliases and copy_model_version instead of stages, database tracking backends instead of ./mlruns, the FastAPI scoring server instead of MLServer/Flask, the split evaluate APIs with explicit threshold gates, and skops/torch.export serialization. Pinned to mlflow 3.15.1; API claims verified against the unpacked mlflow and mlflow-skinny wheels.",
